1
00:00:05,980 --> 00:00:10,780
A boat leaves a harbour and sails on a bearing of 0 7 0 degrees.

2
00:00:10,830 --> 00:00:15,280
That means 70 degrees, turning clockwise from north.

3
00:00:15,330 --> 00:00:17,910
Roughly which way does the boat point?

4
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:21,170
Pause the video and choose.

5
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:24,710
70 degrees is a bit less than 90, which is east.

6
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:29,530
So the boat heads east-north-east, a little north of east.

7
00:00:29,580 --> 00:00:32,570
And what bearing would take it straight back?

8
00:00:32,620 --> 00:00:34,270
We will find out.

9
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:40,170
Remember: north is 0 degrees, east is 90, south is 180, and west is 270.

10
00:00:40,220 --> 00:00:43,360
They are measured clockwise from north.

11
00:00:43,410 --> 00:00:48,660
South-east is halfway between east and south: 135 degrees.

12
00:00:48,710 --> 00:00:52,670
A bearing is the direction of one point from another.

13
00:00:52,720 --> 00:01:01,600
It is measured from north, clockwise, and it is always written with three figures, like 0 7 0, 2 4 5, or 0 0 8.

14
00:01:01,650 --> 00:01:08,230
The bearing of B from A means: stand at A, face north, then turn clockwise until you face B.

15
00:01:08,280 --> 00:01:08,910
Your turn.

16
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:11,090
What is the bearing of due west?

17
00:01:11,140 --> 00:01:12,460
Write three figures.

18
00:01:12,510 --> 00:01:15,700
Pause the video and try it.

19
00:01:15,750 --> 00:01:17,890
Due west is 2 7 0 degrees.

20
00:01:17,940 --> 00:01:19,740
Now, the bearing back.

21
00:01:19,790 --> 00:01:23,690
The bearing of A from B differs by 180 degrees.

22
00:01:23,740 --> 00:01:29,870
If B is 0 4 0 from A, then A is 40 plus 180, which is 2 2 0 from B.

23
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:35,190
If the bearing is more than 180, subtract 180 instead.

24
00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:37,700
3 0 0 becomes 1 2 0.

25
00:01:37,750 --> 00:01:39,030
Here is the method.

26
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:44,320
Step 1: find the point you are measuring from, and draw north there.

27
00:01:44,370 --> 00:01:49,680
Step 2: measure clockwise from north to the line joining the points.

28
00:01:49,730 --> 00:01:53,400
Step 3: write the answer with three figures.

29
00:01:53,450 --> 00:01:58,040
Step 4: for the back bearing, add or subtract 180.

30
00:01:58,090 --> 00:02:02,710
The angle clockwise from north at P to Q is 115 degrees.

31
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:05,720
So the bearing of Q from P is 1 1 5.

32
00:02:05,770 --> 00:02:10,950
The bearing of P from Q is 115 plus 180, which is 2 9 5.

33
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:11,690
Your turn.

34
00:02:11,740 --> 00:02:13,690
A bearing is 0 7 0 degrees.

35
00:02:13,740 --> 00:02:15,540
What is the back bearing?

36
00:02:15,590 --> 00:02:18,580
Pause and work it out.

37
00:02:18,630 --> 00:02:20,260
70 plus 180 is 250.

38
00:02:20,310 --> 00:02:23,290
The back bearing is 2 5 0 degrees.

39
00:02:23,340 --> 00:02:28,190
That takes the boat straight back to the harbour.

40
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:33,110
The angle from north anticlockwise to C, at D, is 40 degrees.

41
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:39,940
Bearings go clockwise, so the bearing is 360 minus 40, which is 3 2 0 degrees.

42
00:02:39,990 --> 00:02:43,990
The angle from north, anticlockwise, to T is 65 degrees.

43
00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:45,650
Sam writes the bearing.

44
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:47,640
Which line is wrong?

45
00:02:47,690 --> 00:02:49,170
Line 1 is wrong.

46
00:02:49,220 --> 00:02:52,230
Bearings are measured clockwise.

47
00:02:52,280 --> 00:02:54,690
360 minus 65 is 295.

48
00:02:54,740 --> 00:02:57,720
The bearing is 2 9 5 degrees.

49
00:02:57,770 --> 00:03:00,660
Pilots and ship captains use bearings.

50
00:03:00,710 --> 00:03:05,360
Airport runways are numbered by their bearing, divided by 10.

51
00:03:05,410 --> 00:03:11,010
A runway pointing on a bearing of about 2 7 0 is called runway 27.

52
00:03:11,060 --> 00:03:18,180
The other end of the same runway points the opposite way, 0 9 0, so it is called runway 9.

53
00:03:18,230 --> 00:03:19,430
One last question.

54
00:03:19,480 --> 00:03:21,650
What is south-west as a bearing?

55
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:23,040
Write three figures.

56
00:03:23,090 --> 00:03:26,320
Pause the video and answer.

57
00:03:26,370 --> 00:03:29,030
South is 180, and west is 270.

58
00:03:29,080 --> 00:03:33,650
South-west is halfway between: 2 2 5 degrees.

59
00:03:33,700 --> 00:03:39,510
To remember: bearings are measured from north, clockwise, with three figures.

60
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:41,970
From A means stand at A.

61
00:03:42,020 --> 00:03:46,990
The back bearing is the bearing plus or minus 180 degrees.

62
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:50,390
Use a protractor and a scale for drawings.

63
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:55,830
Great work! Now practise lesson 14.1 on Camday.
